{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789175037884,"sessionID":"ses_f6cdbab5bffeiOcNlp5LNJFmDc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_ZFHDFy57ql3aDBMRKf2mvnEC","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git status --short"},"output":"(no output)","metadata":{"output":"(no output)","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git status --short","time":{"start":1789175037865,"end":1789175037883}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_06ca1a202f47fecb016aa4a4fdc40c87d190603fbc1e9128ee"}},"id":"prt_093247f7a001pwYmpM3ZYoOzce","sessionID":"ses_f6cdbab5bffeiOcNlp5LNJFmDc","messageID":"msg_093246e170014pn2GZ6zBTzan8"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789175137056,"sessionID":"ses_f6cdbab5bffeiOcNlp5LNJFmDc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_z18UEvZmpTG9SyurbJrE2w9d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Inspect project isolation code","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Inspect repository for project read/update/list authorization and caching plus existing tests/test commands. Research only, no edits. Return relevant files, root causes and recommended minimal fix. Thoroughness medium."},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f6cdb8040ffesSzXchHItbDP0K\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n## Findings\n\n**Three defects are present: unauthorized project reads/updates, cross-organization list-cache collisions, and stale lists after updates.** Existing tests all pass but do not cover these cases. No files were edited; verification used the test runner and in-memory requests only.\n\n### Root causes and relevant files\n\n| Area | File | Finding |\n|---|---|---|\n| Read/update authorization | [project-service.ts:10–29](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts#L10) | `detail(userId, projectId)` ignores `userId`, checking only whether the project exists. `update()` relies on that method for authorization, so any authenticated user can read or rename another organization’s project. |\n| Route authentication | [projects.ts:8–12](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/src/routes/projects.ts#L8) | All three routes require a session, but authentication alone does not establish project ownership access. The missing check belongs in the service. |\n| List-cache isolation | [keys.ts:2–3](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/src/cache/keys.ts#L2) | `projectListKey()` accepts `organizationId` but omits it from the key. Different organizations requesting identical pagination/sorting share cached responses. |\n| Update invalidation | [project-service.ts:24–29](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts#L24) | Successful updates delete only a detail-cache key. Detail responses are not actually cached here, and no list entries are invalidated. Cached names, timestamps, ordering, and page contents remain stale. |\n| Existing authorization helper | [membership.ts:4–5](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/src/auth/membership.ts#L4) | `requireMembership()` already provides the required `403 forbidden` response. |\n| Repository behavior | [project-repository.ts:5–19](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/src/db/project-repository.ts#L5) | List queries correctly filter by organization. Updates modify only `name` and `updatedAt`. The tenant leak is in service authorization/cache keys, not list filtering. |\n| Cache interface | [project-cache.ts:1–15](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/src/cache/project-cache.ts#L1) | Supports `get/set/delete/keys`; values are cloned snapshots. Targeted invalidation can use this existing interface. |\n| Required behavior | [README.md:9–21](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/README.md#L9) | Explicitly requires owning-organization membership, immediate revocation, tenant-separated caching, and invalidation of every list variant for only the updated project’s organization. Organization IDs are opaque strings. |\n\n**Already correct:** list authorization runs before cache lookup on every request. Preserve that ordering: it enforces current membership even on cache hits. It does not prevent the existing collision, because a user authorized for organization B can receive organization A’s cached list.\n\n### Verification\n\nUsing the supplied seed:\n- Alice read `b1`, owned by `org-b`: **200**, exposing the project.\n- Alice renamed `b1`: **200**, modifying another tenant’s project.\n- Organization A and B requests with identical options use the same cache key.\n- After warming organization A’s list and renaming `a1` to `New`, the list still returned **`Alpha`**.\n\n## Recommended minimal fix\n\nLimit production changes to the service and cache-key helpers:\n\n1. **Authorize through `detail()`.**\n   - Fetch the project; preserve `404` if absent.\n   - Call `requireMembership(db, userId, project.organizationId)` before returning it.\n   - Keep `update()` calling this method before validation/mutation.\n   - Use the stored owning organization, never an organization ID from query/body.\n\n2. **Include organization identity in list keys without delimiter ambiguity.**\n   - For example, use an organization prefix such as  \n     ``projects:list:${encodeURIComponent(organizationId)}:``\n     followed by page, page size, sort, and direction.\n   - Share that prefix helper between key generation and invalidation. Encoding plus the terminating delimiter distinguishes IDs with shared prefixes or punctuation.\n\n3. **After a successful update, invalidate every list key with the owning organization’s exact encoded prefix.**\n   - Retain the authorized project returned by `detail()` to obtain its organization.\n   - Iterate `cache.keys()` and delete only matching list entries.\n   - Do not clear unrelated tenants’ entries.\n   - Leave denied/invalid requests free of cache writes/deletions.\n   - Keep caching enabled; no new detail cache or repository redesign is needed.\n\n## Tests and commands\n\n- [package.json:5–10](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/package.json#L5): `npm test` runs `node --test tests/*.test.ts`; Node **24+** required.\n- [projects.test.ts](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/tests/projects.test.ts): five tests covering authorized detail/list/update, anonymous detail, and an invalid name.\n- [account.test.ts](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/tests/account.test.ts): three tests covering health/profile, organization scoping, and logout.\n- **Executed:** `node --test tests/*.test.ts` on Node v24.21.0 — **8 passed, 0 failed**.\n- Focused command: `node --test tests/projects.test.ts`.\n\n### Priority regression coverage\n\n1. Cross-tenant GET/PATCH returns exactly `403 {error:\"forbidden\"}`; denied updates leave storage and cached entries unchanged.\n2. Spoofed organization IDs in body/query cannot authorize access or change ownership; missing projects remain `404`.\n3. Warm A’s list, then request B’s with identical options: each receives only its own projects.\n4. Repeated identical authorized lists reuse cache, verified through `db.counters.projectLists`; each pagination/sorting variant stays distinct.\n5. Revoke membership after warming cache: list, detail, and update are denied immediately.\n6. Updating A invalidates **all** A list variants while B’s cached lists remain hits, including organization IDs sharing prefixes or containing punctuation.\n\nThe existing [app.ts](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/src/app.ts), [database.ts](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/src/db/database.ts), and [membership-repository.ts](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/1-2-opencode/repo/src/db/membership-repository.ts) already expose cache injection, database counters, and membership revocation needed for these tests.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f6cdbab5bffeiOcNlp5LNJFmDc","sessionId":"ses_f6cdb8040ffesSzXchHItbDP0K","model":{"modelID":"gpt-6-astra","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Inspect project isolation code","time":{"start":1789175037888,"end":1789175137053}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_06ca1a202f47fecb016aa4a4fdc42087d1b8175925c0e60938"}},"id":"prt_093247f9c0018hrKH3DYOQYQ5g","sessionID":"ses_f6cdbab5bffeiOcNlp5LNJFmDc","messageID":"msg_093246e170014pn2GZ6zBTzan8"}}
