{"type":"text","timestamp":1789175239780,"sessionID":"ses_f6cdbab5bffeiOcNlp5LNJFmDc","part":{"id":"prt_0932779e1001yegB3X4asSE4jq","messageID":"msg_0932773f40015UCWtfnVxQXqtF","sessionID":"ses_f6cdbab5bffeiOcNlp5LNJFmDc","type":"text","text":"Implemented the organization-isolation fixes.\n\n- **Authorization:** Project reads and updates now require membership in the project’s stored owning organization. Denied requests return the existing `403 forbidden` response without exposing project data or modifying storage. List membership checks remain before cache lookup.\n- **Cache isolation:** List keys now include an encoded organization ID while retaining page, page size, sort, and direction.\n- **Invalidation:** Successful updates invalidate every cached list variant for the owning organization without evicting unrelated organizations’ lists. Caching remains enabled.\n- **Compatibility:** Existing API signatures, response shapes, and status-code conventions are preserved.\n\nAdded `tests/project-isolation.test.ts` covering cross-organization denial, unchanged storage/cache after denied requests, organization switching, membership revocation, pagination/sorting variants, and targeted invalidation for organization IDs with shared prefixes and encoded delimiters.\n\n**Verification**\n- `npm test`: **11 passed, 0 failed**, including all 8 existing tests.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n- Existing tests were not modified; no dependencies were installed.","time":{"start":1789175232993,"end":1789175239779},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0d8c54e799755301016aa4a5c0fc2887d1897a3c88c9274d50","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
